    <DataNode elementId="_1-4-beta-Xylan" textLabel="a (1→4)-β-D-xylan" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="15447" dataSource="ChEBI" />
      <Graphics centerX="391.6453552246094" centerY="178.6086883544922" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="SRI, caspi">|FRAME: 1-4-beta-Xylan &quot; (1&amp;rarr;4)-&amp;beta;-D-xylan&quot;| is a polymer of |FRAME: BETA-D-XYLOSE| residues connected by (1&amp;rarr;4) links. It is found in the cell walls of plants and some green and red algae, and is the major constituent of |FRAME: Hemicelluloses|. Pure xylan, consisting of only xylopyranosyl residues, is rare. Most forms of |FRAME: 1-4-beta-Xylan| are decorated with other types of sugar.</Comment>
